==Battleground==
*1 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawns.
*1 [[Zomboe]] spawns.
*1 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Zomboe]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
*3 [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
*3 [[Dagshund]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The stage plays out how you think it would. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] can be used in the beginning to stall the Heavenly Hippoes, and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] serve as low-cost damage dealers. [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] aren't even necessary since you can just spam meatshields and Can Can Cats to win the level.

Don't use [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]], as all the enemies have the same or superior range to it. And if a Zomboe starts attacking the [[Cat Base]], fire the [[Cat Cannon]] to get it away.

Alternatively, this stage can be rushed fairly easily by landing a double bounty kill on the first Heavenly Hippoe and deploying [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] (preferably with his [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talent]] unlocked) shortly after.

